{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.S5So3WLambdaLift","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.S5So3WLambdaLift","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.route1_closes_iff_ratio_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.route1_closes_iff_ratio_eq","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/S5So3WLambdaLift.lean#L95-L98","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.requiredRatio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.requiredRatio","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/S5So3WLambdaLift.lean#L90-L93","doc":"The exact ratio the near-miss needs: `r* = μ₃ / v_y = 0.4708 / 0.297 ≈ 1.585`.\nRoute 1 closes **iff** the *derived* keystone ratio `r` equals this `r*` — the\nsole empirical question, evaluated forward by the probe (never inverted). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.route1_closes_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.route1_closes_iff","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/S5So3WLambdaLift.lean#L87-L88","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Route1Closes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Route1Closes","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/S5So3WLambdaLift.lean#L80-L85","doc":"**Route-1 closure predicate.**  The A=3 magnitude closes under the keystone\n`W_λ` re-weight iff the `W_λ`-weighted cluster equals `μ₃`:\n`E₀ · h⁴ · (r · κ_y) = μ₃`, equivalently `r · v_y = μ₃` where `v_y = 0.297`.\n`r` is FIXED by `q₀` + hook-lengths (0 fit); a `r` chosen to satisfy this would be\na FIT and is declined. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.clusterMagnitude_reweight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.clusterMagnitude_reweight","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/S5So3WLambdaLift.lean#L71-L76","doc":"**The re-weight ratio scales the magnitude linearly.**  `c₃(W_λ) =\nr · c₃(y_λ)` with `r = κ_W / κ_y`.  So the derived `W_λ` cluster is the\n`y_λ` cluster (`0.297`) times the derived ratio `r` — a forward, 0-fit number. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.clusterMagnitude","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.clusterMagnitude","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/S5So3WLambdaLift.lean#L67-L69","doc":"The physical A=3 cluster magnitude at a block weight is\n`c₃ = E₀ · h⁴ · κ` (the weight's `h⁴`-coefficient at the physical `h`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.reweight_is_coefficient_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.reweight_is_coefficient_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/S5So3WLambdaLift.lean#L54-L65","doc":"**The `y_λ → W_λ` re-weight is a coefficient ratio, never an order change.**\nTwo block weights give deficits `h⁴·κ_y h` and `h⁴·κ_W h`; their ratio is\n`κ_W h / κ_y h` — the shared `h⁴` cancels.  Re-weighting the trace therefore\nrescales the *coefficient* and **cannot** move the leading `h`-order.  (Same\nstructural fact as `BorromeanMagnitudeLift.lift_is_coefficient_ratio`, applied to\nthe block-weight axis rather than the level axis.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.weightedDeficit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.weightedDeficit","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/S5So3WLambdaLift.lean#L48-L52","doc":"A Brunnian-order-suppressed `H₉` cluster deficit at a *given block weight*\n(`y_λ` or `W_λ`) has the shape `D(h) = h⁴ · κ h`, with the weight's `h⁴`-coefficient\n`κ`.  (Cabling preserves the Brunnian order-suppression — probe-measured exponent\n`4.098` — so both weights give an `O(h⁴)` deficit; only `κ` differs.) ","signatureChunk":0}]}